Sat Nov  7 12:48:59 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 0.2.3:
  * New SentencePiece Lite zero-dependency C++20 runtime
    (header-only here; lite/ itself stays disabled)
  * Training: auto character coverage, sparse L1 Unigram pruning,
    custom pretokenizer callback, unk_id=-1 with byte fallback
  * Python: pickling preserves encode options, normalizer flag
    fixes, decode/encode edge cases, buffer-protocol inputs,
    free-threaded fixes; requires Python >= 3.10
  * Performance work plus OSS-Fuzz robustness fixes (bounds checks,
    fuzzer-timeout and input-validation hardening)
  * Removed long-deprecated APIs: SetVocabulary/ResetVocabulary/
    LoadVocabulary, SampleEncodeAndScore*, CalculateEntropy,
    *AsSerializedProto variants, OverrideNormalizerSpec and
    __getstate_for_pickle__; several TrainerSpec fields dropped
    from the spm_train flags
  * C++20 baseline; build against system protobuf 36.2 and flatc
- Packaging: upstream no longer bundles abseil-cpp, so drop
  sentencepiece-use-bundled-abseil.patch (no longer applies) and
  vendor abseil-cpp 20260817.0, the exact upstream pin, for the
  offline FetchContent build instead
- Add sentencepiece-system-flatc.patch (schema header from the
  system flatc, no flatbuffers clone) and
  sentencepiece-link-system-protobuf-lite.patch (link the system
  protobuf-lite into the extension)
- Raise pybind11 floor to >= 2.13 per upstream (built against 3.1;
  upstream caps < 3.1 over a batch-decode slowdown)

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sun Jul 12 19:07:38 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Initial package python-sentencepiece 0.2.2
  * Python bindings for the SentencePiece unsupervised text tokenizer
    and detokenizer for Neural Network-based text generation
  * Add sentencepiece-use-bundled-abseil.patch to build the bundled
    abseil-cpp directly instead of git-cloning it during the build
